$\therefore \int\limits_0^3 {(g(x) - f(x))dx} = \int\limits_0^3 {g(x)dx}  - \int\limits_0^3 {f(x)dx} = \int\limits_0^2 {| - x|dx}  + \int\limits_2^3 { - (x - 4)dx}  - \int\limits_0^2 { - (x - 2)dx}  - \int\limits_2^3 {(x - 2)dx} = \int\limits_0^2 {x\,dx}  - \int\limits_2^3 {(x - 4)dx}  + \int\limits_0^2 {(x - 2)dx}  - \int\limits_2^3 {(x - 2)dx} = $\left[ {{{{$x^2$}} $\over$ 2}} \right]$_0^2 - $\left[ {{{{$x^2$}} $\over$ 2} - 4x} \right]$_2^3 + $\left[ {{{{$x^2$}} $\over$ 2} - 2x} \right]$_0^2 - $\left[ {{{{$x^2$}} $\over$ 2} - 2x} \right]$_2^3 = 2 - \left\{ {\frac{9}{2} - 12 - 2 + 8} \right\} + \{ 2 - 4\}  - \left\{ {\frac{9}{2} - 6 - 2 + 4} \right\} = 2 - \left\{ {\frac{9}{2} - 6} \right\} - 2 - \left\{ {\frac{9}{2} - 4} \right\} = 10 - \frac{9}{2} - \frac{9}{2} = {{20 - 9 - 9} \over 2} = \frac{2}{2} = 1$

